### What happened?

A Solidity call on a typed value gets no `calls` edge: `token.transfer(to, v)` where `IERC20 token`, a cast like `IERC20(addr).transfer(..)`, or `Ownable(x).owner()`. This is the usual way contracts talk to each other. The compiler resolves 74 such calls in OpenZeppelin Contracts v5.4.0 and 725 in solmate (its tests call the contracts under test this way). graphify links 0.

### Steps to reproduce

`IERC20.sol`
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;
interface IERC20 { function transfer(address to, uint256 value) external returns (bool); }
```

`Ownable.sol`
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;
contract Ownable { address private _owner; function owner() public view returns (address) { return _owner; } }
```

`Vault.sol`
```solidity
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;
import {IERC20} from "./IERC20.sol";
import {Ownable} from "./Ownable.sol";
contract Vault {
    IERC20 public token;
    function pay(address to, uint256 v) external { token.transfer(to, v); }
    function payFrom(address t, address to) external { IERC20(t).transfer(to, 1); }
    function ownerOf(address x) external view returns (address) { return Ownable(x).owner(); }
}
```

Then `graphify update .`

### Error output or graph output

No `calls` edges. Expected:
```
pay()     -> transfer()   (IERC20)
payFrom() -> transfer()   (IERC20)
ownerOf() -> owner()      (Ownable)
```

